# ============================================================
# Prettier exclusions for the DeepSeek Harness Plugin Family
# monorepo - adapted to THIS repository's actual structure:
#   Classic/packages/*,
#   EffectTS/packages/* (each with Target/ build dirs),
#   Site/, docs/, Test/, root node_modules + pnpm-lock.
# ============================================================

# Dependencies
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Lockfiles
pnpm-lock.yaml
package-lock.json
yarn.lock

# Build output (per-package Target/ dirs + generic build trees)
Target
**/Target
**/Target/**
target
**/target
**/target/**
dist
**/dist
**/dist/**

# Caches
.cache
**/.cache
.eslintcache
**/.eslintcache
.turbo
**/.turbo

# Markdown is formatted like every other proper file. NOTE: prettier trims
# trailing two-space hard breaks and reflows prose (proseWrap: always), so
# the legacy family prose will re-render once formatted.

# The Site tree - a separate repository with its own prettier config
# (Site/prettier.config.js) and its own .prettierignore, which keeps its
# build output and assets out of formatting; the root's ignore no longer
# hides Site so editors can resolve the site config directly.

# The captured reference shelf - every file under Archive/ and Raw/ is a
# byte-identical copy of an external source, and formatting it would both
# break that guarantee and fail on the archived HTML (inline CSS that
# prettier cannot parse). Curated/ is the project's own prose and IS
# formatted.
Reference/Archive
Reference/Archive/**
Reference/Raw
Reference/Raw/**

# The documentation archive - the historical record. Its documents quote
# illustrative pseudo-code in ```ts / ```css fences that was never valid
# source (a declaration with a comment for an initializer, a CSS shorthand
# with an ellipsis), so the embedded-language printer fails on them. A
# record is not reformatted: the prose stays as written.
Documentation/Archive
Documentation/Archive/**

# The generated static market index - written byte-for-byte by
# Maintain/Generate/Marketplace/Index.mjs; prettier would break its --check.
marketplace.json

# Test fixtures - frozen by design, never reformat
Test
Test/**

# The site's submodule checkout - a second, full copy of THIS repository
# (13,781 files) that the site builds from. It is another repository's working
# tree: formatting it would dirty that checkout, make the site's
# Module/DeepSeek show as modified content, and block `git submodule update`.
Site/Module/DeepSeek
Site/Module/DeepSeek/**

# File types Prettier has no parser for. The CLI skips unknown extensions
# silently when it walks a directory, but the editor passes ONE file and would
# fail with "No parser could be inferred" - listing them here makes Alt+F and
# format-on-save a no-op instead of an error, so the editor and the CLI agree.
**/*.mmd
**/*.svg
**/*.py
**/*.rs

# Scratch space: the derived 0.0.0 placeholder scaffold
# (Maintain/Generate/Placeholders) and one-off probes.
Temporary
Temporary/**
